INSERT INTO "entries" VALUES(11,1,NULL,5,'{"model":[{"role":"system","content":"","sections":{"codemode":"<codemode>\nTools scripts can call (`await tools.<name>(args)`):\n\n### `read`\nRead the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { read(args: {\n  // Maximum number of lines to read\n  limit?: number;\n  // Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)\n  offset?: number;\n  // Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)\n  path: string;\n}): Promise<string | { data: string; mimeType: string; type: \"image\"; }>; };\n```\n\n### `write`\nWrite content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn''t exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { write(args: {\n  // Content to write to the file\n  content: string;\n  // Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)\n  path: string;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `edit`\nEdit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { edit(args: {\n  // One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.\n  edits: Array<{\n    // Replacement text for this targeted edit.\n    newText: string;\n    // Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.\n    oldText: string;\n  }>;\n  // Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)\n  path: string;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `bash`\nRun a shell command; foreground calls auto-background after a short wait, with output capped at 2000 lines/50KB and full logs available through read (use limit for less output). background returns immediately; monitor sends batches that cost model turns. For reminders, use a monitored sleep loop, for example `while sleep 600; do echo \"check X $(date -u +%T)\"; done`; include the check time because repeated identical lines are suppressed. For goals, check a done-condition every few minutes and print a dated reminder only while it is unmet, so the monitor can wake you if you finish a turn early. For watchers, print only when the watched state changes, never heartbeat lines. Stop the monitor’s whole process group when it is no longer needed. Stop reported process groups with kill -- -<pgid>, and at the live-shell limit wait, inspect logs or stop a group instead of launching poll shells.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { bash(args: {\n  // Return immediately with a shell id.\n  background?: boolean;\n  // The shell command to run.\n  command: string;\n  // Inactivity reminder delay in seconds (default 1800); set to 0 to explicitly disable reminders for this shell.\n  // @integer @minimum 0 @maximum 86400\n  inactivityReminderSeconds?: number;\n  // Max output lines (default 2000).\n  // @integer @minimum 1 @maximum 2000\n  limit?: number;\n  // Stream progress batches; set at launch.\n  monitor?: boolean;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `env`\nSet, unset, list or load environment overrides from a dotenv file. Changes apply to subsequent tools and persist across turns/restarts. Values are never printed; unset removes overrides, not ambient defaults. RECURSE_*, PI_* and CHAT_DATA_DIR are protected (16,384 characters/value, 64 KiB total; multiline allowed). No stdin: load requires a file path.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { env(args: {\n  action: \"set\" | \"unset\" | \"list\" | \"load\";\n  // Variable name for set.\n  name?: string;\n  // Variable names for unset.\n  // @minItems 1\n  names?: Array<string>;\n  // Dotenv file path for load, relative to current cwd.\n  path?: string;\n  // Variable value for set; never printed in results.\n  value?: string;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `publish`\nShow files to the operator in the UI: attaches them to your reply and the Files pane; images display inline. Other agents never see published files; to share a file with an agent, send its path. Publishing the same filename adds a version (100 MB/file, 120 files/minute). name renames a single file; path text and links do not publish files.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { publish(args: {\n  name?: string;\n  // @minItems 1\n  paths: Array<string>;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `grep`\nGrep file contents. Smart-case, auto-detects regex vs literal, git-aware. Results are ranked by frecency (most-accessed files first); matches within a file stay in source order. Default limit 20.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { grep(args: {\n  // Force case-sensitive matching. Default uses smart-case (case-insensitive when pattern is all lowercase).\n  caseSensitive?: boolean;\n  // Context lines before+after each match (0-20)\n  context?: number;\n  // Pagination cursor from previous result\n  cursor?: string;\n  // Exclude paths (comma/space-separated or array). Same syntax as path: directory prefix (''test/''), filename with extension (''config.json''), or glob (''*.min.js'', ''**/*.{rs,go}''). A leading ''!'' is optional and ignored — both ''test/'' and ''!test/'' work. Example: ''test/,*.min.js,!vendor/''.\n  exclude?: string | Array<string>;\n  // Max matches (default 20)\n  limit?: number;\n  // Path constraint. Directory prefix (src/ or src/foo/), bare filename with extension (main.rs), or glob (*.ts, src/**/*.cc, {src,lib}/**). Applied to the full repo-relative path. Absolute, ~/, and ../ paths outside the workspace are also supported and searched with a separate index.\n  path?: string;\n  // Search pattern (literal text or regex)\n  pattern: string;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n\n### `find`\nFuzzy path search and glob search. Matches against the whole repo-relative path, not just the filename. Frecency-ranked, git-aware. Multi-word = narrower (AND). Default limit 30.\n\ncodemode tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { find(args: {\n  // Pagination cursor from previous result\n  cursor?: string;\n  // Exclude paths (comma/space-separated or array). Same syntax as path: directory prefix (''test/''), filename with extension (''config.json''), or glob (''*.min.js'', ''**/*.{rs,go}''). A leading ''!'' is optional and ignored — both ''test/'' and ''!test/'' work. Example: ''test/,*.min.js,!vendor/''.\n  exclude?: string | Array<string>;\n  // Max results per page (default 30)\n  limit?: number;\n  // Path constraint. Directory prefix (src/ or src/foo/), bare filename with extension (main.rs), or glob (*.ts, src/**/*.cc, {src,lib}/**). Applied to the full repo-relative path. Absolute, ~/, and ../ paths outside the workspace are also supported and searched with a separate index.\n  path?: string;\n  // Fuzzy filename search and glob search. Frecency-ranked, git-aware. Multi-word = narrower (AND) not bound to order, use for multi word related concept search. Prefer this over ls/find/bash as the first exploration step whenever the user names a concept, feature, or symbol — it surfaces the relevant files in one call. Only use ls/read on a directory when you specifically need the alphabetical layout of an unknown repo, or when a concept search returned nothing.\n  pattern: string;\n}): Promise<string>; };\n```\n</codemode>","preamble":"You are a test agent.","cwd":"<cwd>\n/pi-1.3-fixture/work\n</cwd>","recurse_agent":"<recurse_agent>\nagent\n</recurse_agent>","recurse_memory":"<recurse_memory>\nmemory\n</recurse_memory>","recurse_runtime":"<recurse_runtime>\nruntime\n</recurse_runtime>","recurse_tree":"<recurse_tree>\ntree\n</recurse_tree>","recurse_tools":"<recurse_tools>\ntools\n</recurse_tools>"},"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn''t exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}}},{"name":"compact","description":"Compact your context, especially when changing tasks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"bash","description":"Run a shell command; foreground calls auto-background after a short wait, with output capped at 2000 lines/50KB and full logs available through read (use limit for less output). background returns immediately; monitor sends batches that cost model turns. For reminders, use a monitored sleep loop, for example `while sleep 600; do echo \"check X $(date -u +%T)\"; done`; include the check time because repeated identical lines are suppressed. For goals, check a done-condition every few minutes and print a dated reminder only while it is unmet, so the monitor can wake you if you finish a turn early. For watchers, print only when the watched state changes, never heartbeat lines. Stop the monitor’s whole process group when it is no longer needed. Stop reported process groups with kill -- -<pgid>, and at the live-shell limit wait, inspect logs or stop a group instead of launching poll shells.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"The shell command to run."},"monitor":{"type":"boolean","description":"Stream progress batches; set at launch."},"background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Return immediately with a shell id."},"inactivityReminderSeconds":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":86400,"description":"Inactivity reminder delay in seconds (default 1800); set to 0 to explicitly disable reminders for this shell."},"limit":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"maximum":2000,"description":"Max output lines (default 2000)."}}}},{"name":"wait","description":"Wait for background shells; successive waits/notices use 5m, 10m, 30m, 1h, 3h, then 6h intervals.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"env","description":"Set, unset, list or load environment overrides from a dotenv file. Changes apply to subsequent tools and persist across turns/restarts. Values are never printed; unset removes overrides, not ambient defaults. RECURSE_*, PI_* and CHAT_DATA_DIR are protected (16,384 characters/value, 64 KiB total; multiline allowed). No stdin: load requires a file path.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["action"],"properties":{"action":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","const":"set"},{"type":"string","const":"unset"},{"type":"string","const":"list"},{"type":"string","const":"load"}]},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Variable name for set."},"value":{"type":"string","description":"Variable value for set; never printed in results."},"names":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"description":"Variable names for unset."},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Dotenv file path for load, relative to current cwd."}}}},{"name":"chdir","description":"Change cwd for subsequent tools and turns.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["directory"],"properties":{"directory":{"type":"string","description":"Directory path; relative paths resolve against the current effective cwd"}}}},{"name":"publish","description":"Show files to the operator in the UI: attaches them to your reply and the Files pane; images display inline. Other agents never see published files; to share a file with an agent, send its path. Publishing the same filename adds a version (100 MB/file, 120 files/minute). name renames a single file; path text and links do not publish files.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["paths"],"properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1},"name":{"type":"string"}}}},{"name":"grep","description":"Grep file contents. Smart-case, auto-detects regex vs literal, git-aware. Results are ranked by frecency (most-accessed files first); matches within a file stay in source order. Default limit 20.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"description":"Search pattern (literal text or regex)","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path constraint. Directory prefix (src/ or src/foo/), bare filename with extension (main.rs), or glob (*.ts, src/**/*.cc, {src,lib}/**). Applied to the full repo-relative path. Absolute, ~/, and ../ paths outside the workspace are also supported and searched with a separate index.","type":"string"},"exclude":{"description":"Exclude paths (comma/space-separated or array). Same syntax as path: directory prefix (''test/''), filename with extension (''config.json''), or glob (''*.min.js'', ''**/*.{rs,go}''). A leading ''!'' is optional and ignored — both ''test/'' and ''!test/'' work. Example: ''test/,*.min.js,!vendor/''.","anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"caseSensitive":{"description":"Force case-sensitive matching. Default uses smart-case (case-insensitive when pattern is all lowercase).","type":"boolean"},"context":{"description":"Context lines before+after each match (0-20)","type":"number"},"limit":{"description":"Max matches (default 20)","type":"number"},"cursor":{"description":"Pagination cursor from previous result","type":"string"}}}},{"name":"find","description":"Fuzzy path search and glob search. Matches against the whole repo-relative path, not just the filename. Frecency-ranked, git-aware. Multi-word = narrower (AND). Default limit 30.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["pattern"],"properties":{"pattern":{"description":"Fuzzy filename search and glob search. Frecency-ranked, git-aware. Multi-word = narrower (AND) not bound to order, use for multi word related concept search. Prefer this over ls/find/bash as the first exploration step whenever the user names a concept, feature, or symbol — it surfaces the relevant files in one call. Only use ls/read on a directory when you specifically need the alphabetical layout of an unknown repo, or when a concept search returned nothing.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"Path constraint. Directory prefix (src/ or src/foo/), bare filename with extension (main.rs), or glob (*.ts, src/**/*.cc, {src,lib}/**). Applied to the full repo-relative path. Absolute, ~/, and ../ paths outside the workspace are also supported and searched with a separate index.","type":"string"},"exclude":{"description":"Exclude paths (comma/space-separated or array). Same syntax as path: directory prefix (''test/''), filename with extension (''config.json''), or glob (''*.min.js'', ''**/*.{rs,go}''). A leading ''!'' is optional and ignored — both ''test/'' and ''!test/'' work. Example: ''test/,*.min.js,!vendor/''.","anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"limit":{"description":"Max results per page (default 30)","type":"number"},"cursor":{"description":"Pagination cursor from previous result","type":"string"}}}},{"name":"codemode","description":"Run JavaScript that calls other tools. The input is raw JavaScript (not JSON, no code fence), run as an async function body in a QuickJS sandbox: top-level `await` and `return` work. No Node, file system, network, or timers.\n- `await tools.<name>({ ...args })` resolves to a string, or an object if the tool''s declaration says so, and rejects with an Error on failure. A tool whose declaration returns an object resolves on failure too when it returned that object; check its fields. Calls still running when the script ends are cancelled.\n- The script survives a restart: it resumes where it was, without running finished calls again.\n- Optional first line: `// @options: {\"max_output_tokens\": 10000, \"timeout_ms\": 60000}`\n\nGlobals:\n- `text(value)`, `image(dataUrlOrImageBlock)`, `console.log(...)`, and top-level `return` add output; `exit()` ends the script. With several text items, each starts with a `==> text N/M <==` line, and `console` lines follow the other output in one `<console_output>` block. `image()` also saves the image to a temp file and the result names its path.\n- `store(key, value)` and `load(key)` keep JSON values across codemode calls.\n- `ALL_TOOLS`, `await searchTools(query, { limit?, namespace? })`, `await describeTool(name)`, `await describeNamespace(name)`: find tools the `codemode` section does not list.\n\nThe `codemode` section of the system prompt lists the tools scripts can call, by namespace, as far as space allows.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["code"],"properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"Raw JavaScript source."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"grammar","variants":{"openai_lark":"\nstart: options_source | plain_source\noptions_source: OPTIONS_LINE NEWLINE SOURCE\nplain_source: SOURCE\n\nOPTIONS_LINE: /[ \\t]*\\/\\/ @options:[^\\r\\n]*/\nNEWLINE: /\\r?\\n/\nSOURCE: /[\\s\\S]+/\n"}}}],"timestamp":1793367187808}],"kind":"pi.system","id":11,"conversationId":1,"byTaskId":10}');
